# A3 step 3 planner S5 F1-IX giver index (twow-repo#726; IX-ENTWURF-v0.2, OB-60 pre-review 4376ef95, OB-10 OK 773531cd;
# AiPlayerbot.Planner.GiverIndex / GiverIndexVerify, default 0). Pinned here:
#   (a) GiverIndexPolicy.h is pure (no game type) and has one monotone bucket function used by box and query, widened by kEps;
#   (b) WorldSquare.h: ForEachMapBox hands out exactly the getter values sqOutDistance clamps against (OB-60 1: axes);
#   (c) TravelMgr: the switch is a thread-local pointer, null by default; the index path only for the planner's exact call shape;
#       it is one appendDestinations call (both walk paths unchanged); the radius is the call's maxDistance (OB-10 B1); the built
#       and stale checks run before any index access and the stamp is sized from the built N (OB-10 B2); the portal skip is the F1
#       comparison; the build only at load, after LoadDirectTargets, only with the key on; Clear() resets it first; the giver
#       destinations are created only in LoadQuestTravelTable; no other source file names the switch;
#   (d) PlannerShadow: the switch only around the giver fetch, by a scope that always clears it, with the F1 bound on; the verify
#       runs the configured original after the plan's ms, right before the minute max;
#   (e) the keys: read, GiverIndex above 3 is 0 with one error line, echoed (sorted), documented = 0, in the planner key list;
#       the [PlanTime] index suffix only with the index (OB-10 B3: key 0 leaves the line as before);
#   (f) the unit suite giver_index_policy is registered and runs every test.
# Every check_* returns "" when it holds, else the reason; the negative probes at the end reuse them on mutated text.
